  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Tag with a puck",
  "description": "All the players are inside a box of cones, each with a puck, and must keep skating with it the whole time. Two coaches are the taggers. Anyone touched, or anyone who skates out of the box, is caught and stands still with their legs apart. A free player can rescue a caught team-mate by passing their puck between the team-mate's skates. Start and stop with the whistle and play a few minutes at a time – is everyone caught when time is up?\n\nAs a tagger: tag with your hand, not your stick, and pace yourself so the players win most of the time. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up – then you see both the taggers and your team-mates."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the puck close to the stick when you turn and change direction."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Help each other: rescue a caught team-mate as soon as you can."
    }
  ],
